description:
Design a clock divisor circuit that generates a divided frequency output based on an input clock signal. This module takes an input clock (`clk_in`) and resets the counter when `reset` is asserted. It counts from 0 to a predefined maximum (`M - 1`, where M is set to 8) and, upon reaching the maximum, resets back to 0. The output `div_frec` toggles at half the input clock frequency, effectively providing a frequency division by M, which makes it suitable for generating lower frequency signals from a higher frequency clock.
module top_module(
    output wire div_frec,
    input wire clk_in, reset
    );

code:
module top_module(
    output wire div_frec,
    input wire clk_in, reset
    );localparam N = 1;
localparam M = 8;


reg [N-1:0] divcounter = 0;


always @(posedge clk_in, posedge reset)
	if (reset)
		divcounter <= 0;
	else
		divcounter <= (divcounter == M - 1) ? 0 : divcounter + 1'b1;


assign div_frec = divcounter[N-1];

endmodule

