Design a wait signal generator that produces a random wait signal based on a counter, controlled by an external clock and reset signals. When the WAIT input is active, the module checks the least significant six bits of a 9-bit counter; if they are non-zero, it asserts the wait_random output to HIGH, indicating that a wait condition is met. The counter increments on each clock cycle and resets to zero when the nreset signal is deactivated, allowing for controlled timing during wait conditions.
