description:
Design a PWM (Pulse Width Modulation) signal generator that modulates the output based on an input degree value. The module takes an 8-bit input representing degrees and generates a PWM output (PMW1) tied to a clock signal (CLKOUT1). The PWM output is high when the counter value is less than the sum of the degrees input and an offset of 180, and low otherwise. The counter counts from 0 to 3600, effectively creating a modulation frequency that corresponds to the degree input as a percentage of the total range (360 degrees).
module top_module(
			input CLKOUT1,
			input [7:0]grados,
			output PMW1

			);

code:
module top_module(
			input CLKOUT1,
			input [7:0]grados,
			output PMW1

			);reg [11:0] counter = 0;

always@(posedge CLKOUT1) 
 begin
      if(counter<3600) counter<= counter +1;
      else counter <= 0;
end
assign PMW1 = (counter<(grados+8'b10110100)) ? 1:0;

endmodule

